<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Swaziland Conventions</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1890">1890</a>–<a href="/years/1894">1894</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Swaziland Convention</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eswatini">Swaziland</a> Conventions were three agreements between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and the South African Republic (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transvaal">Transvaal</a>) on the status of Swaziland, concluded in 1890, 1893 and 1894. The first set up a joint administration, while the third made Swaziland a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> of the South African Republic, administered from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pretoria">Pretoria</a> from 1895 without formal incorporation. Britain took over the territory after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-boer-war">Second Boer War</a>.</p></div>
